1
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:12,150
That's it. Get it right to the top.

2
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,590
Steady. Steady.

3
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:50,970
Up she goes.

4
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:53,440
Hey, come on. Put your back into it, huh?

5
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:55,940
Here you are, son.

6
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:01,210
- Oh, gentlemen, please. - To my right.

7
00:01:03,010 --> 00:01:04,630
And you lot, come on. Come on, get it moving.

8
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:05,690
Come on, come on.

9
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:54,270
In all my days I've never seen a man swing an ax like that.

10
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,420
How many men did it take to cut you down?

11
00:03:58,890 --> 00:03:59,830
Just one.

12
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,960
He must have been some kind of monster.

13
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:07,150
He was a woman.

14
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:51,450
I think some of the men are a bit afraid of you.

15
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,810
I'm used to it.

16
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:58,120
When I found you, I thought you'd been dead for days.

17
00:04:59,690 --> 00:05:01,090
The way you were stinking already

18
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:03,190
and you had bugs all over you

19
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:05,680
and bone was coming through right there.

20
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,740
I was gonna give you a proper burial and then you coughed.

21
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:13,600
Oh, nearly shit myself.

22
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:17,580
I reckoned you were gonna die by the time I loaded you on the wagon,

23
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:18,540
but you didn't.

24
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:21,590
Now, I reckoned you'd die a dozen more times over the next few days,

25
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:23,880
but you didn't. What kept you going?

26
00:05:28,190 --> 00:05:29,260
Hate.

27
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:33,640
No, there's a reason you're still here.

28
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,300
Aye, there's a reason. I'm a big fucker and I'm tough to kill.

29
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,730
No, a reason.

30
00:05:39,660 --> 00:05:41,480
Gods aren't done with you yet.

31
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,830
I've heard that before.

32
00:05:45,630 --> 00:05:47,830
Man was talking about a different god, though.

33
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:49,740
Well, maybe he was right.

34
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,690
I don't know much about the gods.

35
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,210
You're in the wrong line of work.

36
00:05:54,210 --> 00:05:55,940
Oh, there's plenty of pious sons of bitches

37
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:58,700
who think they know the word of god or gods.

38
00:05:58,710 --> 00:06:01,630
I don't. I don't even know their real names.

39
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:05,350
Maybe it is the Seven. Or maybe it's the old gods.

40
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:07,680
Or maybe it's the Lord of Light.

41
00:06:07,690 --> 00:06:10,310
Or maybe they're all the same fucking thing.

42
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:11,630
I don't know.

43
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:14,610
What matters, I believe,

44
00:06:14,610 --> 00:06:16,860
is that there's something greater than us.

45
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:21,660
And whatever it is, it's got plans for Sandor Clegane.

46
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:28,120
You didn't know me back in my time.

47
00:06:30,270 --> 00:06:32,110
You don't know the things I've done.

48
00:06:34,010 --> 00:06:35,590
I've heard stories.

49
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:39,360
If the gods are real...

50
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,770
why haven't they punished me?

51
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:47,890
They have.

52
00:07:03,570 --> 00:07:04,540
Your Grace.

53
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:07,400
What are we reading today?

54
00:07:08,330 --> 00:07:10,410
The Book of the Mother, Your Holiness.

55
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,320
Chapter three, verse 12.

56
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,630
"As water rounds the stones, smoothing--"

57
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:20,490
"Smoothing what was jagged, so does a woman's love

58
00:07:20,490 --> 00:07:22,980
calm a man's brute nature.

59
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:25,730
A wife salves her husband's wounds,

60
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:28,250
a mother sings her son to sleep."

61
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,330
You learn quickly.

62
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:34,930
There are some who know every verse of the sacred text,

63
00:07:35,710 --> 00:07:38,590
but don't have a drop of the Mother's mercy in their blood

64
00:07:38,590 --> 00:07:41,750
and savages who can't read at all

65
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:44,200
who understand the Father's wisdom.

66
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:52,050
For years I pretended to love the poor, the afflicted.

67
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:56,240
I had pity for them, but I never loved them.

68
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,610
They disgusted me.

69
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:01,880
They are hard to love.

70
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:05,030
The poor disgust us because they are us,

71
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,880
shorn of our illusions.

72
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:10,980
They show us what we'd look like without our fine clothes.

73
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:13,100
How'd we smell without perfume.

74
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:18,630
Can I ask you about a personal matter?

75
00:08:19,610 --> 00:08:20,720
Of course.

76
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:26,820
The king mentioned that since your reunion,

77
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:29,440
you haven't joined him in the marriage bed.

78
00:08:30,890 --> 00:08:31,810
No.

79
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:34,230
You have a duty, Your Grace.

80
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:37,720
To your husband, your king, your country,

81
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:40,180
to the gods themselves.

82
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,060
It's just...

83
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:47,210
the desires that once drove me no longer do.

84
00:08:48,850 --> 00:08:51,150
Congress does not require desire

85
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:54,540
on the woman's part, only patience.

86
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,990
The king must have an heir

87
00:08:58,570 --> 00:09:00,930
if we are to continue our good work.

88
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,350
Forgive me.

89
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:06,480
Sometimes the true path is hard to find.

90
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,020
Hard to find

91
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:11,220
and harder still to walk upon.

92
00:09:12,350 --> 00:09:14,340
But you've made great progress.

93
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,420
I only pray your grandmother follows your lead.

94
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:23,290
My grandmother?

95
00:09:24,330 --> 00:09:25,330
Yes.

96
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:28,130
The Queen of Thorns is a remarkable woman,

97
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:29,260
a strong woman,

98
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:32,210
and an unrepentant sinner.

99
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,130
You must teach her the new way

100
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,520
as she taught you the old.

101
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,210
Or I fear for her safety,

102
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:41,090
body and soul.

103
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:48,750
Does it move or talk?

104
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:51,450
I want to speak with you alone.

105
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:54,810
Septa Unella has been my true friend and counselor.

106
00:09:54,810 --> 00:09:56,830
Oh, this is madness!

107
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:06,810
You're not in your sanctuary now, my dear.

108
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,010
All I have to do is whistle

109
00:10:08,010 --> 00:10:10,630
and my men will stroll in here and bash you about...

110
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:13,110
- Grandmother. - ...until I tell them to stop.

111
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:15,160
If I tell them to stop.

112
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:18,930
- You could use a good bashing. - Grandmother, please.

113
00:10:18,930 --> 00:10:20,240
What have they done to you?

114
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:22,280
You marched against the High Sparrow,

115
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,360
- against the Faith. - We marched for you.

116
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:27,240
The gods could have punished you and Father, but they didn't.

117
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,100
- They showed mercy. - And what about your brother?

118
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,880
What mercy did they show him?

119
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:35,070
Loras's only hope is to confess his crimes and repent.

120
00:10:35,070 --> 00:10:38,200
If he does, the Faith will allow him to return to Highgarden.

121
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:40,570
He'll have to renounce his name and title...

122
00:10:40,570 --> 00:10:43,310
- Have you lost your mind? - ...and live his life as a penitent.

123
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:46,920
He is the heir to Highgarden, the future of House Tyrell.

124
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,260
He can begin again.

125
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,100
As a mindless fanatic.

126
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,650
As a free man.

127
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,650
You will leave for Highgarden today.

128
00:10:55,770 --> 00:10:58,360
There is no law that says you must stay here.

129
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:01,330
I am the queen.

130
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:05,090
It is my duty to serve my husband the king.

131
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:10,990
But you should leave, Grandmother.

132
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:13,060
Your place is at home.

133
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:16,200
I will never leave you. Never.

134
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,340
You must.

135
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:21,920
Go home.

136
00:11:23,210 --> 00:11:26,070
Find comfort in prayer and good works.

137
00:11:29,090 --> 00:11:31,040
The Mother watches over us all.

138
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,200
I'll see you soon, my dear.

139
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,560
Seven blessings to you, Grandmother.

140
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:01,380
Shall we pray?

141
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:20,730
We said we'd fight with you, King Crow,

142
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,090
when the time comes and we meant it,

143
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:25,120
but this isn't what we agreed to.

144
00:12:25,230 --> 00:12:26,670
These aren't white walkers.

145
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:28,410
This isn't an army of the dead.

146
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:30,840
This isn't our fight.

147
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:35,000
If it weren't for him, none of us would be here.

148
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:38,600
All of you would be meat in the Night King's army.

149
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:41,630
And I'd be a pile of charred bones just like Mance.

150
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,270
Remember Mance's camp?

151
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:46,460
It stretched all the way to the horizon.

152
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:48,210
And look at us now.

153
00:12:48,850 --> 00:12:50,380
Look what's left of us.

154
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:54,050
And if we lose this, we're gone.

155
00:12:54,730 --> 00:12:58,440
Dozens of tribes, hundreds of generations.

156
00:12:58,930 --> 00:13:00,590
Be like we were never there at all.

157
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:03,000
We'll be the last of the free folk.

158
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,480
That's what'll happen to you if we lose.

159
00:13:09,610 --> 00:13:12,220
The Boltons, the Karstarks, the Umbers,

160
00:13:12,550 --> 00:13:13,890
they know you're here.

161
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:17,060
They know that more than half of you are women and children.

162
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:19,580
After they finish with me, they'll come for you.

163
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,390
You're right.

164
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:23,700
This isn't your fight.

165
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,720
You shouldn't have to come to Winterfell with me.

166
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:28,260
I shouldn't be asking you.

167
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,230
It's not the deal we made.

168
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:34,170
I need you with me if we're going to beat them,

169
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:37,270
and we need to beat them if you're going to survive.

170
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:45,980
The crows killed him because he spoke for the free folk

171
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:47,800
when no other southerners would.

172
00:13:48,890 --> 00:13:50,340
He died for us.

173
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:56,100
If we are not willing to do the same for him, we're cowards.

174
00:13:57,070 --> 00:13:58,500
And if that's what we are,

175
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,600
we deserve to be the last of the free folk.

176
00:14:18,710 --> 00:14:19,970
Snow.

177
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:04,500
Are you sure they'll come?

178
00:15:06,450 --> 00:15:08,570
We're not clever like you southerners.

179
00:15:08,930 --> 00:15:12,150
When we say we'll do something, we do it.

180
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,440
I heard you were leaving King's Landing.

181
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,090
That is hardly your concern.

182
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:37,730
Your grandson is still a prisoner.

183
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:39,500
You'll leave him rotting in a cell?

184
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,690
Loras rots in a cell because of you.

185
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:46,470
The High Sparrow rules this city because of you.

186
00:15:46,470 --> 00:15:50,840
Our two ancient houses face collapse because of you

187
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:53,070
and your stupidity.

188
00:15:54,530 --> 00:15:55,880
You're right.

189
00:15:57,470 --> 00:15:58,790
I made a terrible mistake.

190
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:00,840
I carry it with me every single day.

191
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:02,260
Good.

192
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:05,290
I delivered an army of fanatics onto our doorstep.

193
00:16:06,110 --> 00:16:07,970
And now we must fight them together.

194
00:16:10,790 --> 00:16:12,190
We need each other.

195
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:17,800
I wonder if you're the worst person I've ever met.

196
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,610
At a certain age, it's hard to recall.

197
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:25,210
But the truly vile do stand out through the years.

198
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:27,890
Do you remember the way you smirked at me

199
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:31,470
when my grandson and granddaughter were dragged off to their cells?

200
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,820
I do. I'll never forget it.

201
00:16:34,970 --> 00:16:36,600
You love your granddaughter.

202
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:39,330
I love my son.

203
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,880
It's the only truth I know.

204
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,410
We must defend them.

205
00:16:45,610 --> 00:16:48,500
I'm leaving this wretched city as fast as I can

206
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:52,630
before that shoeless zealot throws me into one of his cells.

207
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:54,700
If you're half as bright as you think you are,

208
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:56,540
you'll find a way out of here, too.

209
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:57,690
Never.

210
00:16:58,160 --> 00:16:59,760
I'll never leave my son.

211
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:01,840
What'll you do, then?

212
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:04,880
You have no support. Not anymore.

213
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:08,340
Your brother's gone. The High Sparrow saw to that.

214
00:17:08,470 --> 00:17:10,990
The rest of your family have abandoned you.

215
00:17:10,990 --> 00:17:12,960
The people despise you.

216
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,610
You're surrounded by enemies, thousands of them.

217
00:17:15,610 --> 00:17:17,740
You're going to kill them all by yourself?

218
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:20,770
You've lost, Cersei.

219
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:24,480
It's the only joy I can find in all this misery.

220
00:17:32,370 --> 00:17:33,860
Pick the pace up.

221
00:17:34,870 --> 00:17:36,130
Keep going.

222
00:17:40,390 --> 00:17:41,840
Keep it moving!

223
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,700
Now, that is a sorry attempt at a siege.

224
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:24,250
Someone needs to teach those sad twats how to dig trenches.

225
00:18:24,250 --> 00:18:26,350
Someone certainly does.

226
00:18:27,650 --> 00:18:29,960
Oh, no. Not me.

227
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:31,790
I'm just an upjumped sellsword.

228
00:18:31,790 --> 00:18:34,510
You're an anointed knight. There's quite a difference.

229
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:36,500
Aye, knights don't get paid.

230
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,170
You have better instincts than any officer

231
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:39,510
in the Lannister army.

232
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:42,100
That's like saying I have a bigger cock

233
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:44,260
than anyone in the Unsullied army.

234
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:48,790
I expect to command all the Lannister forces before long.

235
00:18:49,510 --> 00:18:51,360
You can be the right hand I lost.

236
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:58,050
You promised me a lordship and a castle

237
00:18:58,050 --> 00:19:00,250
and a highborn beauty for a wife.

238
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:02,840
And you'll get all three. A Lannister always--

239
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:06,040
Don't say it. Don't fucking say it.

240
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,640
Come out and fight us, Blackfish.

241
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:30,210
We have Lord Edmure.

242
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:34,860
Yield the castle or we'll hang him.

243
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:55,730
This is your last warning.

244
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:58,330
Yield the castle.

245
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:12,340
You think I won't do it, old man?

246
00:20:15,610 --> 00:20:18,130
I sliced your niece's throat from ear to ear.

247
00:20:18,130 --> 00:20:21,790
And where were you? Running and hiding like a fucking coward.

248
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:28,730
Yield the castle or I cut his throat.

249
00:20:38,490 --> 00:20:41,590
Go on, then. Cut his throat.

250
00:21:03,170 --> 00:21:04,460
Lothar, is it?

251
00:21:06,150 --> 00:21:07,410
Ser Jaime.

252
00:21:08,220 --> 00:21:09,640
We didn't know you were coming.

253
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,500
'Cause you didn't set a proper perimeter.

254
00:21:11,530 --> 00:21:14,880
You just allowed 8,000 men to approach unchallenged.

255
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,190
Good thing we're friends

256
00:21:16,190 --> 00:21:18,290
or we'd be fucking you in the ass right now.

257
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:20,380
Have Lord Edmure bathed and fed.

258
00:21:22,710 --> 00:21:23,920
Walder.

259
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:29,080
Edmure is a prisoner of House Frey.

260
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:34,730
Only a fool makes threats he's not prepared to carry out.

261
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:37,560
Now let's say I threatened to hit you

262
00:21:37,650 --> 00:21:40,400
unless you shut your mouth, but you kept talking.

263
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,860
- What do you think I'd do? - I don't give a rat's--

264
00:21:45,310 --> 00:21:47,990
I'm here by the king's command to take back this castle.

265
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:50,050
Have him bathed and fed.

266
00:21:50,550 --> 00:21:52,390
Unless you'd like to take his place.

267
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:56,030
Apologies, Ser Jaime.

268
00:21:56,030 --> 00:21:57,330
Do as he says.

269
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:59,620
The siege is now under my command.

270
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,560
The next time the Blackfish looks out from those ramparts,

271
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:05,830
he'll see an army at his gates, not whatever this is.

272
00:22:05,830 --> 00:22:08,010
Have your lads start digging perimeter trenches.

273
00:22:08,010 --> 00:22:09,570
Set pickets every hundred yards.

274
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:12,220
And work double-time on those siege towers and trebuchets.

275
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:13,510
Those are our siege towers--

276
00:22:13,510 --> 00:22:16,440
As I said, the siege is under my command.

277
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:18,820
If that's not to your liking, go home.

278
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:26,960
Get word to the Blackfish.

279
00:22:27,690 --> 00:22:28,830
I want a parley.

280
00:22:29,470 --> 00:22:30,950
A parley or a fight?

281
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:34,050
He's an old man.

282
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:35,810
You've got one hand.

283
00:22:36,310 --> 00:22:37,900
My money's on the old boy.

284
00:22:57,850 --> 00:22:59,150
Lady Mormont.

285
00:23:00,690 --> 00:23:02,440
Welcome to Bear Island.

286
00:23:09,730 --> 00:23:11,830
I remember when you were born, my lady.

287
00:23:12,010 --> 00:23:13,770
You were named for my Aunt Lyanna.

288
00:23:13,810 --> 00:23:16,410
It was said she was a great beauty. I'm sure you will be, too.

289
00:23:16,410 --> 00:23:18,950
I doubt it. My mother wasn't a great beauty

290
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:20,560
or any other kind of beauty.

291
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,280
She was a great warrior, though.

292
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,510
She died fighting for your brother Robb.

293
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:32,070
I served under your uncle at Castle Black, Lady Lyanna.

294
00:23:32,070 --> 00:23:34,930
He was also a great warrior and an honorable man.

295
00:23:34,930 --> 00:23:36,770
I was his steward. In fact--

296
00:23:36,770 --> 00:23:39,870
I think we've had enough small talk. Why are you here?

297
00:23:42,510 --> 00:23:45,280
Stannis Baratheon garrisoned at Castle Black

298
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:47,600
before he marched on Winterfell and was killed.

299
00:23:47,750 --> 00:23:49,390
He showed me the letter you wrote to him

300
00:23:49,390 --> 00:23:50,560
when he petitioned for men.

301
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:52,510
- It said-- - I remember what it said.

302
00:23:52,650 --> 00:23:55,310
Bear Island knows no king but the King in the North

303
00:23:55,310 --> 00:23:56,760
whose name is Stark.

304
00:23:59,500 --> 00:24:01,090
Robb is gone,

305
00:24:01,530 --> 00:24:03,280
but House Stark is not.

306
00:24:03,530 --> 00:24:06,290
And it needs your support now more than ever.

307
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:10,300
I've come with my sister to ask for House Mormont's allegiance.

308
00:24:22,060 --> 00:24:24,000
As far as I understand, you're a Snow

309
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,670
and Lady Sansa is a Bolton.

310
00:24:26,090 --> 00:24:27,710
Or is she a Lannister?

311
00:24:27,970 --> 00:24:29,840
I've heard conflicting reports.

312
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,160
I did what I had to do to survive, my lady.

313
00:24:33,510 --> 00:24:36,210
But I am a Stark. I will always be a Stark.

314
00:24:36,210 --> 00:24:38,770
If you say so. In any case,

315
00:24:38,770 --> 00:24:41,690
you don't just want my allegiance. You want my fighting men.

316
00:24:41,690 --> 00:24:44,800
Ramsay Bolton cannot be allowed to keep Winterfell, my lady.

317
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:46,420
It is our duty to stop him.

318
00:24:46,430 --> 00:24:50,280
Even more so because he holds our brother Rickon Stark as prisoner.

319
00:24:53,570 --> 00:24:55,380
What you have to understand, my lady, is that--

320
00:24:55,380 --> 00:24:58,000
I understand that I'm responsible for Bear Island

321
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,330
and all who live here.

322
00:24:59,330 --> 00:25:00,830
So why should I sacrifice

323
00:25:00,830 --> 00:25:03,770
one more Mormont life for someone else's war?

324
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:11,320
If it please, my lady,

325
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:14,410
I understand how you feel.

326
00:25:14,790 --> 00:25:17,200
I don't know you, Ser...?

327
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:19,320
Davos, my lady, of House Seaworth.

328
00:25:19,550 --> 00:25:21,490
You needn't ask your maester about my house.

329
00:25:21,490 --> 00:25:23,010
It's rather new.

330
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:28,500
All right, Ser Davos of House Seaworth.

331
00:25:28,550 --> 00:25:30,600
How is it you understand how I feel?

332
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:34,290
You never thought you'd find yourself in your position.

333
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:38,700
Being responsible for so many lives at such a young age.

334
00:25:38,790 --> 00:25:40,640
I never thought I'd be in my position.

335
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:44,060
I was a crabber's son, then I was a smuggler.

336
00:25:45,370 --> 00:25:47,730
And now I find myself addressing the lady of a great house

337
00:25:47,730 --> 00:25:49,020
in time of war.

338
00:25:49,530 --> 00:25:53,760
But I'm here because this isn't someone else's war.

339
00:25:54,930 --> 00:25:56,280
It's our war.

340
00:25:58,410 --> 00:26:00,050
Go on, Ser Davos.

341
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:04,380
Your uncle, Lord Commander Mormont,

342
00:26:04,410 --> 00:26:06,450
made that man his steward.

343
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:09,260
He chose Jon to be his successor because he knew

344
00:26:09,260 --> 00:26:11,520
he had the courage to do what was right,

345
00:26:11,810 --> 00:26:13,850
even if it meant giving his life.

346
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:18,480
Because Jeor Mormont and Jon Snow both understood

347
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:22,070
that the real war isn't between a few squabbling houses.

348
00:26:23,030 --> 00:26:25,700
It's between the living and the dead.

349
00:26:26,850 --> 00:26:28,890
And make no mistake, my lady,

350
00:26:29,570 --> 00:26:31,040
the dead are coming.

351
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:35,050
Is this true?

352
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:39,720
Your uncle fought them at the Fist of the First Men.

353
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:41,380
I fought them at Hardhome.

354
00:26:42,330 --> 00:26:43,800
We both lost.

355
00:26:45,010 --> 00:26:48,770
As long as the Boltons hold Winterfell, the North is divided.

356
00:26:48,890 --> 00:26:52,710
And a divided North won't stand a chance against the Night King.

357
00:26:54,260 --> 00:26:57,160
You want to protect your people, my lady. I understand.

358
00:26:57,290 --> 00:26:59,080
But there's no hiding from this.

359
00:26:59,580 --> 00:27:03,570
We have to fight and we need to do it together.

360
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:18,190
House Mormont has kept faith with House Stark for 1,000 years.

361
00:27:21,290 --> 00:27:23,440
We will not break faith today.

362
00:27:28,470 --> 00:27:30,470
Thank you, my lady.

363
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:33,600
How many fighting men can we expect?

364
00:27:40,270 --> 00:27:41,600
62.

365
00:27:45,070 --> 00:27:47,960
- 62? - We are not a large house,

366
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:49,310
but we're a proud one.

367
00:27:49,310 --> 00:27:51,150
And every man from Bear Island

368
00:27:51,150 --> 00:27:53,720
fights with the strength of 10 mainlanders.

369
00:27:54,430 --> 00:27:57,230
If they're half as ferocious as their lady,

370
00:27:57,230 --> 00:27:59,020
the Boltons are doomed.

371
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:17,180
Kingslayer.

372
00:29:18,420 --> 00:29:19,680
Blackfish.

373
00:29:20,030 --> 00:29:21,950
I assume you're here

374
00:29:22,270 --> 00:29:25,000
to fulfill the vow you gave my niece.

375
00:29:25,270 --> 00:29:27,940
I don't see Sansa and Arya.

376
00:29:27,990 --> 00:29:30,260
- I don't have them. - Pity.

377
00:29:31,230 --> 00:29:33,880
Do you wish to resume your captivity?

378
00:29:35,260 --> 00:29:36,410
Then why are you here?

379
00:29:36,410 --> 00:29:37,960
You know why I'm here.

380
00:29:38,410 --> 00:29:40,330
This castle belongs to House Frey.

381
00:29:40,330 --> 00:29:41,810
You're trespassing.

382
00:29:41,810 --> 00:29:44,690
In the name of King Tommen, I order you to surrender or--

383
00:29:44,690 --> 00:29:46,930
Or you'll kill Edmure?

384
00:29:48,470 --> 00:29:51,200
My nephew's marked for death no matter what.

385
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:52,760
Hang him and be done with it.

386
00:29:52,760 --> 00:29:54,450
It won't stop with Edmure.

387
00:29:54,460 --> 00:29:56,420
You'll force me to storm the castle.

388
00:29:56,420 --> 00:29:57,940
Hundreds will die.

389
00:29:58,490 --> 00:30:02,040
Hundreds of mine. Thousands of yours.

390
00:30:02,040 --> 00:30:04,390
If you can breach the walls.

391
00:30:04,820 --> 00:30:08,850
We'll breach them and kill every last one of you.

392
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:11,780
But if you surrender,

393
00:30:12,350 --> 00:30:14,390
I'll spare the lives of your men.

394
00:30:14,870 --> 00:30:16,210
On my honor.

395
00:30:16,340 --> 00:30:18,130
Your honor?

396
00:30:18,130 --> 00:30:21,620
Bargaining with oathbreakers is like building on quicksand.

397
00:30:21,620 --> 00:30:23,260
The war is over, ser.

398
00:30:23,420 --> 00:30:26,400
Why sacrifice living men to a lost cause?

399
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:36,050
As long as I'm standing, the war is not over.

400
00:30:36,740 --> 00:30:38,660
This is my home.

401
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:42,630
I was born in this castle and I'm ready to die in it.

402
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:45,130
So you can either attack

403
00:30:45,910 --> 00:30:48,250
or try to starve us out.

404
00:30:49,090 --> 00:30:51,600
We have enough provisions for two years.

405
00:30:53,330 --> 00:30:56,970
Do you have two years, Kingslayer?

406
00:31:02,450 --> 00:31:05,530
You clearly have no intention of saving your men's lives.

407
00:31:05,950 --> 00:31:07,710
Why did you come treat with me?

408
00:31:08,310 --> 00:31:10,170
Sieges are dull.

409
00:31:10,830 --> 00:31:14,220
And I wanted to see you in person, get the measure of you.

410
00:31:15,420 --> 00:31:16,800
Well, now you have.

411
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:19,140
Aye, now I have.

412
00:31:19,700 --> 00:31:21,560
I'm disappointed.

413
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,260
The answer is no.

414
00:31:33,260 --> 00:31:35,940
- Lord Glover, if you could just hear us out. - I've heard enough.

415
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:39,020
We've only just taken back this castle from the ironborn.

416
00:31:39,020 --> 00:31:41,000
The Boltons helped us do it.

417
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:43,080
Now you want me to fight against them?

418
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:45,140
I could be skinned for even talking to you.

419
00:31:45,140 --> 00:31:47,430
The Boltons are traitors. Roose Bolton--

420
00:31:47,430 --> 00:31:50,670
Have other northern houses pledged to fight for you?

421
00:31:51,530 --> 00:31:52,950
House Mormont.

422
00:31:54,250 --> 00:31:55,430
And?

423
00:31:56,430 --> 00:31:58,090
We sent ravens to Houses Manderly--

424
00:31:58,090 --> 00:31:59,870
I don't care about ravens.

425
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:03,560
You're asking me to join your army.

426
00:32:03,590 --> 00:32:06,470
Who is fighting in this army?

427
00:32:12,280 --> 00:32:14,750
The bulk of the force is made up of wildlings.

428
00:32:17,910 --> 00:32:19,640
Then the rumors are true.

429
00:32:21,220 --> 00:32:22,950
I didn't dare believe them.

430
00:32:27,070 --> 00:32:30,060
I received you out of respect for your father.

431
00:32:30,450 --> 00:32:32,420
Now I would like you to leave.

432
00:32:32,460 --> 00:32:35,720
House Glover will not abandon its ancestral home

433
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:38,510
to fight alongside wildlings.

434
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:42,430
- Lord Glover. - There's nothing else to say.

435
00:32:42,430 --> 00:32:44,350
I would remind you that House Glover

436
00:32:44,350 --> 00:32:46,800
is pledged to House Stark.

437
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:49,370
Sworn to answer when called upon.

438
00:32:59,590 --> 00:33:03,710
Yes, my family served House Stark for centuries.

439
00:33:03,780 --> 00:33:07,010
We wept when we heard of your father's death.

440
00:33:07,010 --> 00:33:09,270
When my brother was lord of this castle,

441
00:33:09,370 --> 00:33:13,570
he answered Robb's call and hailed him King in the North.

442
00:33:18,250 --> 00:33:20,890
And where was King Robb

443
00:33:21,070 --> 00:33:23,700
when the Ironborn attacked this castle?

444
00:33:23,940 --> 00:33:27,630
When they threw my wife and children in prison

445
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:31,040
and brutalized and killed our subjects?

446
00:33:32,350 --> 00:33:35,270
Taking up with a foreign whore.

447
00:33:35,490 --> 00:33:39,580
Getting himself and those who followed him killed.

448
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,720
I served House Stark once,

449
00:33:46,770 --> 00:33:49,080
but House Stark is dead.

450
00:34:47,780 --> 00:34:49,420
Why did we have to come here?

451
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:52,090
Some of us still like it.

452
00:34:56,780 --> 00:34:58,510
Have a drink at least.

453
00:34:58,510 --> 00:34:59,820
I don't want one.

454
00:35:01,900 --> 00:35:03,370
Don't go far, love.

455
00:35:05,170 --> 00:35:06,700
I'll find you in a bit.

456
00:35:12,070 --> 00:35:14,980
Nothing on the Iron Islands has an ass like that.

457
00:35:16,050 --> 00:35:17,930
Doesn't interest you anymore?

458
00:35:20,890 --> 00:35:23,990
I'm sorry. I won't joke about it.

459
00:35:25,860 --> 00:35:27,720
I'll never hurt you, little brother.

460
00:35:28,260 --> 00:35:29,740
Don't you know that?

461
00:35:33,490 --> 00:35:35,580
You think Uncle Euron's hunting for us?

462
00:35:35,590 --> 00:35:38,920
Of course he is. As long as we're alive, we're a threat.

463
00:35:39,340 --> 00:35:40,790
He'll find us.

464
00:35:40,890 --> 00:35:43,500
It's a great big world and we have fast ships.

465
00:35:43,640 --> 00:35:44,790
Drink.

466
00:35:45,180 --> 00:35:46,540
I don't want any.

467
00:35:46,540 --> 00:35:48,840
I don't care what you want. Drink.

468
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:53,040
Drink it all.

469
00:35:56,390 --> 00:36:00,110
You're Ironborn, Theon. I know you've had some bad years.

470
00:36:00,110 --> 00:36:01,230
Some bad years?

471
00:36:01,230 --> 00:36:04,220
But I'm tired of watching you cower like a beat dog.

472
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:06,470
Drink the goddamn ale.

473
00:36:11,050 --> 00:36:12,540
Now listen to me.

474
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,370
I need you.

475
00:36:14,390 --> 00:36:16,260
The real Theon Greyjoy,

476
00:36:16,260 --> 00:36:18,020
not this rat shit pretender.

477
00:36:18,180 --> 00:36:19,760
Can you find him for me?

478
00:36:21,220 --> 00:36:22,430
Drink.

479
00:36:24,650 --> 00:36:26,330
You escaped. You hear me?

480
00:36:26,420 --> 00:36:28,850
You got away and you're never going back.

481
00:36:29,160 --> 00:36:30,650
We'll get justice for you.

482
00:36:30,660 --> 00:36:31,560
If I got justice,

483
00:36:31,560 --> 00:36:33,580
my burnt body would hang over the gates of Winterfell.

484
00:36:33,580 --> 00:36:36,280
Fuck justice, then. We'll get revenge. Drink.

485
00:36:41,030 --> 00:36:42,270
Listen to me.

486
00:36:43,080 --> 00:36:45,820
If you're so broken that there's no coming back,

487
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:48,690
take a knife and cut your wrists.

488
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:50,900
End it.

489
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:55,470
But if you're staying, Theon, I need you.

490
00:36:56,330 --> 00:36:58,290
We're gonna sail to Meereen.

491
00:36:58,510 --> 00:37:01,300
We're gonna make a pact with this Dragon Queen.

492
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:04,750
And we're gonna take back the Iron Islands.

493
00:37:07,430 --> 00:37:08,960
Are you with me?

494
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:12,560
Are you really with me?

495
00:37:30,730 --> 00:37:34,440
Now, since it's my last night ashore for a long while,

496
00:37:34,440 --> 00:37:36,660
I'm gonna go fuck the tits off this one.

497
00:37:48,510 --> 00:37:51,220
Stannis camped here on his way to Winterfell.

498
00:37:51,930 --> 00:37:53,540
And that's a good thing?

499
00:37:54,450 --> 00:37:57,330
He was the most experienced commander in Westeros.

500
00:37:57,520 --> 00:37:59,450
He chose this place for a reason.

501
00:38:00,200 --> 00:38:02,490
Those mountains are a natural fortification.

502
00:38:02,490 --> 00:38:04,370
There's a stream down there for the horses.

503
00:38:04,370 --> 00:38:05,980
We're not staying here long.

504
00:38:06,160 --> 00:38:07,960
Another storm could hit any day.

505
00:38:07,960 --> 00:38:10,820
Aye, the snows defeated Stannis

506
00:38:10,820 --> 00:38:12,550
as much as the Boltons did.

507
00:38:13,020 --> 00:38:16,330
We have to march on Winterfell now while we still can.

508
00:38:17,170 --> 00:38:18,850
2,000 wildlings,

509
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:22,110
200 Hornwoods, 143 Mazins--

510
00:38:22,110 --> 00:38:23,980
62 Mormonts.

511
00:38:24,940 --> 00:38:26,510
It's not what we'd hoped for.

512
00:38:28,100 --> 00:38:31,960
But we still have a chance if we're careful and smart.

513
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:35,790
For fuck's sake.

514
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:41,660
So he's your most trusted advisor now?

515
00:38:42,140 --> 00:38:45,460
Because he secured 62 men from a 10-year-old?

516
00:38:45,460 --> 00:38:47,910
Ser Davos is the reason I'm standing here talking to you

517
00:38:47,910 --> 00:38:50,250
and he served Stannis for years.

518
00:38:50,310 --> 00:38:53,070
Stannis who lost the Blackwater,

519
00:38:53,070 --> 00:38:55,700
who murdered his own brother, who doesn't have a head?

520
00:38:56,510 --> 00:38:59,670
It's not enough. We need more men.

521
00:39:01,030 --> 00:39:02,220
There's no time.

522
00:39:02,220 --> 00:39:04,350
If we went down to Castle Cerwyn, I know that Lord--

523
00:39:04,380 --> 00:39:06,680
We fight with the army we have.

524
00:39:09,980 --> 00:39:12,040
Friends, this is not worth fighting over!

525
00:39:14,260 --> 00:39:15,510
This'll be it, now.

526
00:39:15,510 --> 00:39:17,320
Right, now we don't need to be fighting--

527
00:39:18,260 --> 00:39:19,700
- Who the fuck are you? - Hold on.

528
00:39:19,710 --> 00:39:21,010
Yeah, who the fuck are you?

529
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:08,250
I was a soldier once.

530
00:40:08,550 --> 00:40:11,390
All my superiors thought I was brave.

531
00:40:11,740 --> 00:40:14,830
I wasn't. I mean, I never ran from a fight.

532
00:40:15,010 --> 00:40:18,230
Only because I was afraid my friends would see I was afraid.

533
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:20,080
That's all I was, a coward.

534
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:24,180
We followed orders no matter the orders.

535
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:26,140
Burn that village.

536
00:40:26,480 --> 00:40:29,270
Fine, I'm your arsonist.

537
00:40:29,270 --> 00:40:32,250
Steal that farmer's crops. Good, I'm your thief.

538
00:40:32,250 --> 00:40:35,910
Kill those young lads so they won't take up arms against us.

539
00:40:37,540 --> 00:40:39,000
I'm your murderer.

540
00:40:40,190 --> 00:40:43,220
I remember once a woman screaming at us,

541
00:40:43,220 --> 00:40:46,780
calling us animals as we dragged her son from their hut.

542
00:40:47,790 --> 00:40:49,240
But we weren't animals.

543
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:52,300
Animals are true to their nature

544
00:40:53,030 --> 00:40:54,830
and we had betrayed ours.

545
00:40:57,780 --> 00:41:00,550
I cut that young boy's throat myself

546
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:02,540
as his mother screamed

547
00:41:02,790 --> 00:41:04,820
and my friends held her back.

548
00:41:08,110 --> 00:41:09,170
That night...

549
00:41:11,890 --> 00:41:13,470
I felt such shame.

550
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:16,820
Shame was so heavy on me,

551
00:41:16,820 --> 00:41:19,990
I couldn't eat, I couldn't sleep.

552
00:41:20,750 --> 00:41:23,400
All I could do was stare into that dark sky

553
00:41:23,500 --> 00:41:26,760
and listen to that mother screaming her son's name.

554
00:41:32,580 --> 00:41:35,020
I'll hear her screaming the rest of my life.

555
00:41:39,560 --> 00:41:41,580
Now, I know I can never bring that lad back.

556
00:41:41,580 --> 00:41:43,960
All I can do with time I've got left

557
00:41:44,060 --> 00:41:46,750
is bring a little goodness into the world.

558
00:41:46,750 --> 00:41:48,620
That's all any of us can do, isn't it?

559
00:41:48,750 --> 00:41:51,150
Never too late to stop robbing people,

560
00:41:51,150 --> 00:41:52,960
to stop killing people.

561
00:41:53,030 --> 00:41:54,740
Start helping people.

562
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:58,360
It's never too late to come back.

563
00:42:13,190 --> 00:42:16,710
And it's not about waiting for the gods to answer your prayers.

564
00:42:16,710 --> 00:42:19,530
It's not even about the gods. It's about you.

565
00:42:20,480 --> 00:42:23,350
Learning you have to answer your prayers yourself.

566
00:42:26,450 --> 00:42:28,300
Seven save you, friends.

567
00:42:30,370 --> 00:42:31,500
How can we help you?

568
00:42:35,210 --> 00:42:36,450
What are you doing here?

569
00:42:37,130 --> 00:42:39,050
Well, we're talking about life.

570
00:42:40,120 --> 00:42:40,900
You?

571
00:42:41,510 --> 00:42:43,020
Protecting the people.

572
00:42:43,590 --> 00:42:45,700
Well, we thank you for your protection.

573
00:42:46,950 --> 00:42:48,790
Who are you protecting us from?

574
00:42:51,550 --> 00:42:52,900
Do you have any horses?

575
00:42:53,750 --> 00:42:54,960
No horses.

576
00:42:55,170 --> 00:42:57,640
No gold. No steel.

577
00:42:58,410 --> 00:43:01,800
Food, then. Protecting the people is hungry work.

578
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:03,120
I'm sure it is.

579
00:43:04,020 --> 00:43:05,800
You're welcome to stay for supper,

580
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:07,580
but we have hungry mouths here.

581
00:43:15,630 --> 00:43:16,870
Stay safe.

582
00:43:18,070 --> 00:43:20,210
The night is dark and full of terrors.

583
00:43:44,190 --> 00:43:46,140
"Seven save you, friends."

584
00:43:47,470 --> 00:43:50,070
I'm a fucking septon. What was I supposed to say?

585
00:43:50,070 --> 00:43:51,190
They don't believe in your Seven.

586
00:43:51,190 --> 00:43:53,810
They're from the Brotherhood. They follow the Red God.

587
00:43:53,810 --> 00:43:55,360
Aye, well, all are welcome here.

588
00:43:56,350 --> 00:43:57,960
Anyway, we got nothing for them.

589
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:59,660
Sure, you do. You've got food,

590
00:43:59,660 --> 00:44:01,890
you've got steel even if you say you don't.

591
00:44:02,590 --> 00:44:03,760
And you've got women.

592
00:44:03,870 --> 00:44:06,380
What do you want to do? Fight them?

593
00:44:06,790 --> 00:44:07,640
Kill them?

594
00:44:08,220 --> 00:44:09,860
It'd be you against all of them.

595
00:44:09,860 --> 00:44:12,200
I mean, these people don't know how to fight.

596
00:44:12,690 --> 00:44:13,630
You do.

597
00:44:14,310 --> 00:44:16,010
I'm done with fighting.

598
00:44:16,230 --> 00:44:18,270
Even if it's to protect yourself?

599
00:44:19,160 --> 00:44:20,820
Violence is a disease.

600
00:44:21,520 --> 00:44:24,460
You don't cure a disease by spreading it to more people.

601
00:44:25,650 --> 00:44:27,930
You don't cure it by dying, either.

602
00:44:30,220 --> 00:44:31,630
You've done enough work for one day.

603
00:44:31,630 --> 00:44:33,070
Come on up for some supper.

604
00:44:34,890 --> 00:44:36,590
It's gonna be a cold night.

605
00:44:37,030 --> 00:44:38,440
We'll need firewood.

606
00:44:39,220 --> 00:44:40,760
I'll save you a bowl of stew.

607
00:44:41,760 --> 00:44:43,810
Might even have some ale hidden away.

608
00:44:52,300 --> 00:44:53,700
He's not a lying man.

609
00:44:53,900 --> 00:44:55,970
He says the Iron Fleet's in Slaver's Bay.

610
00:44:55,970 --> 00:44:57,390
I'm inclined to believe him.

611
00:44:58,000 --> 00:45:00,610
I'm not going anywhere near those mad fuckers.

612
00:45:00,610 --> 00:45:02,060
You're Westerosi.

613
00:45:02,570 --> 00:45:03,710
What do you care?

614
00:45:04,280 --> 00:45:05,810
I want to book passage home.

615
00:45:07,090 --> 00:45:09,510
You? Can't afford it.

616
00:45:17,110 --> 00:45:18,380
Where'd you steal this from?

617
00:45:18,380 --> 00:45:19,360
Why do you care?

618
00:45:20,900 --> 00:45:22,180
We leave in two days.

619
00:45:22,980 --> 00:45:24,780
You can have a hammock in steerage.

620
00:45:27,170 --> 00:45:28,330
I want a cabin.

621
00:45:29,030 --> 00:45:30,270
And we'll leave at dawn.

622
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:33,370
See you at sunrise.

623
00:45:54,590 --> 00:45:55,800
Sweet girl.

